<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  What a station can make. The kitchen's one recipe (design 48 section 5), then the smelter's two
  (design 62 section 9). A RecipeHandle is a position in PawnContent.FromDefs's list, appended,
  never inserted: a bill stores it.

  Any raw food, 500 of it by nutrition, into one meal of 900: a-18's simple meal exactly. That is
  three carrots (540) or ten pieces of meat; what is over stays in the pan for the next meal. A
  pan with any meat in it makes Item_CookedMeal, one with none Item_VegetableMeal, and a burnt
  one Item_BurntMeal whatever went in.

  300 ticks at the galley, divided by the cook's speed (Work_Cooking): five seconds at level 10,
  twelve and a half for a novice. The campfire takes twice as long, burns half as often again,
  and swallows one wood a meal - it has no hopper, so the wood is fetched like an ingredient.

  burnPerMilleByLevel is the owner's shape (interview #4: about 30 per cent at 0, 5 at 8, none
  from 14), one entry a level; a level past the end reads the last, which is 0.
-->
<Defs>

  <RecipeDef>
    <defName>Recipe_Meal</defName>
    <label>cook a meal</label>
    <workTicks>300</workTicks>
    <ingredientNutrition>500</ingredientNutrition>
    <product>Item_CookedMeal</product>
    <productNoMeat>Item_VegetableMeal</productNoMeat>
    <burntProduct>Item_BurntMeal</burntProduct>
    <burnPerMilleByLevel>
      <li>300</li><li>250</li><li>200</li><li>160</li><li>130</li>
      <li>100</li><li>80</li><li>65</li><li>50</li><li>40</li>
      <li>30</li><li>20</li><li>10</li><li>5</li><li>0</li>
    </burnPerMilleByLevel>
    <stations>
      <!-- The galley, BuildingHandle 12. -->
      <li>
        <building>12</building>
      </li>
      <!-- The campfire, BuildingHandle 8: twice the time, half as many burns again, one wood (item 2). -->
      <li>
        <building>8</building>
        <workFactorPerMille>2000</workFactorPerMille>
        <burnFactorPerMille>1500</burnFactorPerMille>
        <fuelItem>2</fuelItem>
        <fuelCount>1</fuelCount>
      </li>
    </stations>
  </RecipeDef>

  <!--
    THE SMELTER'S TWO (design 62 section 9). A crafted recipe names its ingredients and products
    item by item, which is what tells it from the kitchen's: Workshop works these, Kitchen never
    sees them, and the food fields above mean nothing here.

    Ten ore into five bars, both metals alike. Iron ore comes up fifteen to a cut cell (Ores.xml),
    so a cell is a batch and a half; a steel wall's five bars are ten ore. 450 ticks at the
    standard pace, divided by the smelter's crafter's speed (Work_Crafting, on Construction):
    seven and a half seconds at level 10, the galley's meal and a half.

    fuelPerBatch 3 is in the smelter's hopper worth (Buildings.xml, Building_Smelter's
    hopperFuels: coal 3, wood 1), so a batch burns one coal or three wood. Coal is the better fuel
    because it is worth three times as much, and that is said once, on the building. INVENTED.
  -->
  <RecipeDef>
    <defName>Recipe_SmeltIron</defName>
    <label>smelt iron</label>
    <workTicks>450</workTicks>
    <ingredients>
      <li><item>Item_IronOre</item><count>10</count></li>
    </ingredients>
    <products>
      <li><item>Item_IronBar</item><count>5</count></li>
    </products>
    <stations>
      <!-- The smelter, BuildingHandle 15. -->
      <li>
        <building>15</building>
        <fuelPerBatch>3</fuelPerBatch>
      </li>
    </stations>
  </RecipeDef>

  <RecipeDef>
    <defName>Recipe_SmeltCopper</defName>
    <label>smelt copper</label>
    <workTicks>450</workTicks>
    <ingredients>
      <li><item>Item_CopperOre</item><count>10</count></li>
    </ingredients>
    <products>
      <li><item>Item_CopperBar</item><count>5</count></li>
    </products>
    <stations>
      <li>
        <building>15</building>
        <fuelPerBatch>3</fuelPerBatch>
      </li>
    </stations>
  </RecipeDef>

</Defs>
